namespace Eigen {

/** \page Bibliography Bibliography

The published sources the headers cite with `\ref`, one anchor per work, named by first author and year as
EmrysFilter's bibliography names them (design/decisions.md [bibliography-page]). A comment that cites an entry says
what the code takes from it, such as the equation numbers or the section, and where it departs. Entries are in
alphabetical order by first author.

\anchor Barrau2017
A. Barrau and S. Bonnabel. The invariant extended Kalman filter as a stable observer. *IEEE
Transactions on Automatic Control*, 62(4):1797–1812, 2017. The left- and right-invariant extended
Kalman filters and the group-affine dynamics on which their error's Jacobian does not depend on
the estimate. Free: [arXiv](https://arxiv.org/abs/1410.1465). Not read; cited as EmrysFilter's
bibliography cites it, through \ref Sola2018 "Solà, Deray, and Atchuthan (2018)".

\anchor Hartley2020
R. Hartley, M. Ghaffari, R. M. Eustice, and J. W. Grizzle. Contact-aided invariant extended Kalman
filtering for robot state estimation. *The International Journal of Robotics Research*,
39(4):402–430, 2020. The invariant filter of an inertial unit on \f$ SE_2(3) \f$, and of a legged
robot whose state keeps each foot in contact inside the group. Free:
[arXiv](https://arxiv.org/abs/1904.09251). Not read; the library takes no algorithm from it.

\anchor Hertzberg2013
C. Hertzberg, R. Wagner, U. Frese, and L. Schröder. Integrating generic sensor fusion algorithms
with sound state representations through encapsulation of manifolds. *Information Fusion*,
14(1):57–77, 2013. Free: [arXiv](https://arxiv.org/abs/1107.1119).

\anchor Kalman1960
R. E. Kalman. A new approach to linear filtering and prediction problems. *Journal of Basic
Engineering*, 82(1):35–45, 1960.

\anchor Markley2003
F. L. Markley. Attitude error representations for Kalman filtering. *Journal of Guidance,
Control, and Dynamics*, 26(2):311–317, 2003. The text checked is the NASA preprint of 2002
(NTRS 20020060647), whose reset section says the reset leaves the covariance unchanged. Free:
[NASA preprint](https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20020060647).

\anchor Mueller2017
M. W. Mueller, M. Hehn, and R. D'Andrea. Covariance correction step for Kalman filtering with an
attitude. *Journal of Guidance, Control, and Dynamics*, 40(9):2301–2306, 2017. The text checked
is the authors' preprint.

\anchor Sola2017
J. Solà. Quaternion kinematics for the error-state Kalman filter. Technical report,
arXiv:1711.02508, 2017. §6.3, the ESKF reset, eqs. (284) to (288) and (294). Free:
[arXiv](https://arxiv.org/abs/1711.02508).

\anchor Sola2018
J. Solà, J. Deray, and D. Atchuthan. A micro Lie theory for state estimation in robotics.
Technical report IRI-TR-18-01, arXiv:1812.01537, 2018 (version 9, 2021). Appendix B, the right
Jacobian of SO(3), eq. (143). Free: [arXiv](https://arxiv.org/abs/1812.01537).

*/

}
